; The dscheck tests of the TLS session (design section 2.19). The test copies
; src/tls/weft_tls.ml with no interface, and the traced Atomic and the Domain
; with a spin limit of test/dscheck. Its own modules Weft and Weft_flow are
; models of the parts of weft that the session uses: Fiber.Mutex is a spin
; lock on traced atomics, with the cancellation points of the real mutex, and
; a flow reads and writes strings. Thus dscheck examines the real code of the
; session in each order of its locks and of its atomic status. FreeBSD and
; Windows in CI have no tls: the build_if skips the test there.

(copy_files#
 (files ../../src/tls/weft_tls.ml))

(copy_files#
 (files ../dscheck/{atomic,domain}.ml))

(copy_files#
 (files ../tls/tls_support.{ml,mli}))

(test
 (name test_dscheck_tls)
 (package weft-tls)
 (build_if %{lib-available:weft-tls})
 (libraries dscheck tls x509 domain-name ipaddr mirage-crypto-rng ptime))
